The canonical JaCaMo metamodel, mapping, verification resources and Auction example
included here are the exact files audited by this repository's release tests.

The plugin JAR embeds JSON Schema Validator 2.0.1 (NetworkNT), itu 1.14.0,
Jackson 2.18.3, and SnakeYAML 2.3 under Apache License 2.0. It also embeds
SLF4J API 2.0.17 under its MIT license. The corresponding license texts are
in licenses/APACHE-2.0.txt and licenses/SLF4J-MIT.txt. Jackson and its
FastDoubleParser third-party notices and license texts remain in the JAR's
META-INF resources.

The opt-in USE4GOAL_OBSERVED_V1 profile embeds selected original CSL/iStar
sources from use4Goal, upstream commit
6f3e73801239fd8bfb94ca8d04ba531b903c0ac9. Original package names, copyright
headers, source hashes and upstream paths are retained in
provenance/use4goal-provenance.json (also META-INF/use4goal-provenance.json
inside the plugin). The original contextual seam patch is P-CTX-01; its
diff and the separate native USE printer adapter changes are included in
provenance/. No full legacy goal plugin, legacy CSL runtime backend or
solver is installed. Corresponding selected source and build inputs are
in use-jacamo-semantic-engine/ in this repository; see the provenance README.

ANTLR 4.9.3 runtime and parser generator are pinned to the same version.
The ANTLR Project copyright and BSD-3-Clause license are retained in
licenses/ANTLR4-4.9.3.txt, copied from the upstream 4.9.3 tag:
https://raw.githubusercontent.com/antlr/antlr4/4.9.3/LICENSE.txt
USE's separate ANTLR 3 runtime remains owned by the USE host.
